<title>JAPAN: Japan April copper cable orders up, shipments down.</title>
<headline>Japan April copper cable orders up, shipments down.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese copper wire and cable orders climbed 4.5 percent in April from the same month last year, while shipments slipped 1.2 percent, the Japanese Electric Wire and Cable Makers' Association said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The preliminary April data and revised March data were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   April 97     yr/yr change    March 97 (revised)</p>
<p>Orders	   94,100	 +4.5 pct	  93,584  (+5.2 pct)</p>
<p>  Exports	 4,500	 +0.4 pct	   5,527 (-17.9 pct)</p>
<p>Shipments	88,400	 -1.2 pct	  96,971  (+4.1 pct)</p>
<p>  Construction 30,900	 -2.4 pct	  36,079 (+16.6 pct)</p>
<p>  Electrical   23,200	 -0.9 pct	  24,916  (+4.9 pct)</p>
<p>  Elec Power   11,200	 -4.1 pct	  11,245 (-17.5 pct)</p>
<p>  Automobile    5,900	+14.1 pct	   6,807 (+11.4 pct)</p>
<p>  Telecomms     4,200	-12.1 pct	   3,934 (-16.7 pct)</p>
<p>  Exports	 4,600	 +0.8 pct	   6,305  (-6.5 pct)</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
